WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:15.129
This man is worth 5,564,800,000 Berries. How
much is that you ask? Given that one berry

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:20.900
is pretty much the same as one yen, and one
hundred yen are about 1 American dollar, that

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:27.810
would make Gol D. Roger's head worth 55,648,000
million Dollars. In other words, catching

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:35.410
Roger would have bought you this nice little
yacht, about 1500 bitcoins or 55 million pieces

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:41.180
of okay-tasting gum. Something, which sounds
like a Mr. Beast Video.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:47.100
Unsurprisingly, it is by far the highest bounty
we have seen in the story so far, an with

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.890
the notable exceptions of Luffy and his father
dragon, there doesn't seem to be anyone out

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:57.660
there who will ever be able to match it. As
the first pirate king and the only known captain

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.550
to ever reach the end of the grand line, it
is to be expected that Roger would have a

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:17.270
high bounty, but being a great adventurer
and notorious pirate alone, doesn't explain

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:22.109
a bounty that in the One Piece world would
basically make you royalty. The reason Gold

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:27.639
Roger was so infamous and dangerous to the
world government lies within his character,

00:01:27.639 --> 00:01:32.689
that tells us a lot about where Luffy is heading
in the story as well. It's a story about freedom.

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:39.220
About power. About camaraderie. About Politics,
History and the most infamous treasure in

00:01:39.220 --> 00:02:08.599
the world, the One Piece itself. This is the
story of Gol D. Roger.

00:02:08.599 --> 00:02:15.320
Roger's character was inspired by two real
pirates, Olivier Levasseur and Henry Every.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:20.700
Leavesseur became known for tossing a cryptogram
from his execution platform into the crowd,

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.670
telling them, that the hidden message on it
would lead them to his gigantic treasure,

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:31.640
that to this day hasn't been found. This of
course directly parallels Roger's legendary

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:37.890
speech at his execution. - But it also seems
like a likely inspiration for the poneglyphs,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:42.470
stones written in a forgotten language, that
lead to the last island of the grand line,

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:53.200
laugh tale, where the one piece is hidden.
Every on the other hand, became famous for

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:59.270
being the richest pirate in the world, earning
him the epithet 'king of the pirates'. Despite

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:05.380
having the highest bounty in history of around
$700,000 USD in today's currency, placed on

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:10.680
his head, he vanished with the legendary treasure
he accumulated over his life in the Caribbean,

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:18.980
which at that time used to be known as the
new world. He was the inspiration for a new

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:23.270
generation of notorious pirates, including
Blackbeard,&nbsp;Bartholomew Roberts,&nbsp;Calico

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:29.150
Jack,&nbsp;Samuel Bellamy&nbsp;and&nbsp;Edward Low, among
others, who were children at the time. And

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:34.740
I know what you're thinking now: Ohara - This
dude's nose looks just like a Dong. Well,

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:39.540
why do you think he became one of the most
violent pirates of all time. Exactly, because

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:46.680
of comments like that. Stop it!

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:51.600
## Roger's role within the story is extremely
interesting in many ways. He quite literally

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:58.600
is a legendary pirate, in the sense that his
tale is a story whiting the story. By doing

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:04.709
so, Oda advances his own world building, introduces
the inspiration for Luffy and many other characters,

00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:10.540
while at the same time drawing a number of
parallels between the nested story and the

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:16.850
main story line. Roger's character, right
form the start explains why so many people

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:22.180
in this world are pirates, next to the injustice
of the world government of course. Interestingly

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:27.620
enough, the more we learn about him and the
people around him, unlike in many other stories,

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:33.889
where the real deal can't live up to the legend,
in Roger's case, he becomes even more impressive

00:04:33.889 --> 00:04:40.189
a person the more we learn about him. One
of the strongest and most free-spirited characters

00:04:40.189 --> 00:04:46.010
in the story, not bound by anything or anyone.
And of course the more we learn about him,

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:56.400
the more we see the parallels between him
and Luffy.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.439
First of all I think it's really interesting
to see that the apparently unattainable goal

00:05:00.439 --> 00:05:05.449
that Luffy has at the beginning of the story,
in other words, becoming pirate king, has

00:05:05.449 --> 00:05:10.699
already been achieved by this other legendary
character. In fact, all the things that come

00:05:10.699 --> 00:05:15.219
with the title, that usually should be unique
to the main character of the story, have all

00:05:15.219 --> 00:05:20.210
been done before. Finding Laugh Tale at the
end of the grand line, learning the true history

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:25.699
of the world and discovering the biggest treasure
out there - literally from the get-go we are

00:05:25.699 --> 00:05:31.830
being told that all of these things have already
been achieved by some other dude 20 years

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:39.240
ago. Kind of unexciting for Luffy to then
just repeat what Roger already did. However,

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:44.219
when you really think about it, what it pretty
much guarantees for us, is that Luffy will

00:05:44.219 --> 00:05:50.719
in some shape or form overcome Roger and his
legacy. He will do what even the first pirate

00:05:50.719 --> 00:05:59.199
king could not do, which most likely is change
the unjust world order.

00:05:59.199 --> 00:06:07.699
We actually know for a fact, that while both
Luffy and Roger share the same dream, this

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:12.789
dream is not actually becoming pirate king,
that title didn't even exist before Roger

00:06:12.789 --> 00:06:17.460
in the first place. Rather, whatever this
dream is, it will have something to do with

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:25.669
the main theme of the story: Freedom. And
while Roger managed to live a life of freedom

00:06:25.669 --> 00:06:30.909
with his crew, Luffy will be the one to bring
it to everyone, in whatever shape or form

00:06:30.909 --> 00:06:36.029
that will be. That's why the parallels between
them are so important. The same hat inherited

00:06:36.029 --> 00:06:41.270
from Roger, the same will of D both carry
in their name, the voices of all things, their

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:46.419
inclusive and quirky crews and even parts
of their personality seem to match, as Luffy

00:06:46.419 --> 00:06:58.760
and Roger share a number of lines throughout
the story. Hell, when you look at adult Luffy,

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:04.730
he even looks like Roger. At the same time
of course, they aren't the same person. As

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:11.259
we have seen throughout the Oden flashback
in Wano, while similar, Luffy and Roger are

00:07:11.259 --> 00:07:16.680
still different people and Luffy certainly
is the turned-version of some of the traits

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:19.659
that made Roger so special in the first place.

00:07:19.659 --> 00:07:25.009
As we now know, Roger was waiting for someone
like Luff&nbsp;to appear. - Most likely after

00:07:25.009 --> 00:07:29.819
abandoning his crew in anticipation of his
death, he instructed his remaining crew to

00:07:29.819 --> 00:07:45.620
look for the one who could become the new
pirate king and finish what he couldn't. Crocus

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:52.369
and Rayleigh are positioned suspiciously strategically
at the entrances of the grand line and the

00:07:52.369 --> 00:07:58.449
new world respectively, keeping an eye out
for whoever enters. And both go them make

00:07:58.449 --> 00:08:03.469
explicit comparisons between Roger and Luffy.
- And then of course there is Shanks, who

00:08:03.469 --> 00:08:09.030
surely didn't bet his arm on a little boy
on a whim. He is certain that Luffy will ring

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:23.069
in a new age. So, it's extremely likely Roger
entrusted him with his hat, to find his successor

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:33.300
and entrust that hat to him in return. -

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:38.890
And this is already the first reason that
Roger earned himself this ridiculous bounty

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:45.150
of 5,5 Billion Berry. Being the only known
person in the story so far to rave laugh tale

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:50.770
and learn the real history, he possesses knowledge
that the world government has actively tried

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:56.301
to eradicate for centuries. And not in the
nice, 'hey let's all not talk about it anymore'

00:08:56.301 --> 00:09:01.840
sort of way, but more as in, if you so much
as try to learn about the past, we will come

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:08.541
with our magma psychopath and burn your whole
darn island to the ground - sort of way. As

00:09:08.541 --> 00:09:13.120
Rayleigh tells us, Roger and his crew learned
about the true history, which without any

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:28.131
other factors involved would already save
him a top position on the bounty board. Just

00:09:28.131 --> 00:09:32.040
look at what happened to Robin when she was
not even a teenager.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:37.900
But on top of that, Roger had both the intend
to act upon that knowledge AND the power to

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:43.080
actually do so. I mean the guy clashed with
anyone who is known to be strong in the story:

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:51.500
Garp, WHitebeard, Kaido, Shiki, Big Mom, Rocks
himself. What a god damn monster. --

